  "question": {
    "text": "A box is put on a scale which is adjusted to read zero , when the box is empty. A stream of pebbles is then poured into the base from a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;above its bottom at a rate of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> pebbles/s. Each pebble has a mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>. If the pebbles collide with the box such that they immediately come to rest after collision, then the scale reading at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> after the pebbles begin to fill the box is [ neglect piling up of pebbles]&nbsp;",
